  "description": "This application has been prepared by Common Ground Workshop Ltd in support of a Householder Planning Application for roof alterations and a loft conversion at 13 Langley Drive, Wanstead, London E11, within the London Borough of Redbridge.\n\nThe proposal seeks planning permission for the conversion of the existing roof space to provide additional habitable accommodation. The works comprise a hip-to-gable roof enlargement, a rear dormer extension to the principal roof slope, a dormer extension to the rear outrigger roof slope, associated rooflights, and alterations to the ground floor rear fenestration.\n\nThe scheme was originally designed and submitted as an application for a Certificate of Lawful Development (Proposed) under Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). Following assessment by the Local Planning Authority, it was determined that the cumulative volume of the proposed roof enlargement, including the hip-to-gable extension, exceeds the 50 cubic metre threshold permitted under Class B. As a result, planning permission is required.\n\nThis statement describes the site and its surroundings, outlines the proposed development and design rationale, and demonstrates that the proposal accords with relevant national, regional and local planning policy.\n",
